# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Event Management — Client Portal
#
# Copy to `.env.local` for local development, or paste these into your host's
# environment settings (Vercel: Project → Settings → Environment Variables).
#
# Both variables are NEXT_PUBLIC_, which means they are INLINED INTO THE
# BROWSER BUNDLE at build time. Never put a secret behind that prefix — anyone
# viewing source can read it. Nothing here is a secret, and nothing else should
# be added here that is.
#
# Because they are baked in at BUILD time, changing either one in the host's
# dashboard does nothing until you redeploy.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# REQUIRED. The Event Management admin backend, INCLUDING the /api/v1 prefix.
# Leaving the prefix off produces 404s on every call with no other symptom.
#
#   local  http://localhost:5001/api/v1
#   live   https://event-management-admin-backend.onrender.com/api/v1
NEXT_PUBLIC_API_URL=https://event-management-admin-backend.onrender.com/api/v1

# OPTIONAL (V2). The tenant's public website — NOT this portal. No trailing slash.
#
# V2 has no public website: sign-in lives in THIS portal at /login, so nothing
# needs this to sign in. It only feeds the footer links (Help Center, Terms) and
# the "Create a new account" link on the account-deleted page; they are hidden
# when it is unset. Leave it out on V2.
#
#   V1  https://event-managment-public-website.vercel.app
# NEXT_PUBLIC_SITE_URL=

# OPTIONAL. Google Maps key for the venue map in Create / Edit Event — the same
# key as the mobile app. In Google Cloud it needs "Maps JavaScript API" enabled
# (and "Places API (New)" for the search box), and its restrictions must allow
# this site. Unset, the Venue step shows typed latitude / longitude only.
NEXT_PUBLIC_GOOGLE_MAPS_API_KEY=
